## Manufacturing Parameters & Boundary Conditions## 1. LAYER 1: Communication & Cognitive Layer (Raspberry Pi 5)

* Vertical Clearance (To Top Shell): 1.5 mm (Filled with high-conductivity indium or silicone thermal pads for seamless heat transfer to the chassis).
* Routing Constraints: All co-axial cable lengths from the UWB/920MHz RF front-ends to the top-mounted antennas must be under 30 mm to prevent impedance mismatch and signal attenuation.
* Thermal Management: Dissipates processing heat directly through the Top Aluminum Shell to the outer environment via the air-gap insulated outer skin, preventing thermal throttling.

## 2. EMI Shield Bulkhead (Isolation Barrier)

* Material: 0.5 mm thick nickel-plated copper plate, mechanically grounded directly to the main structural chassis GND.
* Function: Physically blocks high-frequency electromagnetic interference (EMI) generated by Layer 3's high-current motor drivers from penetrating Layer 1's high-speed memory bus (LPDDR5), preventing data bit-flips and OS crashes.

## 3. LAYER 2: Real-Time Signal Processing Layer (STM32H7)

* Concentric Alignment: Centered exactly along the concentric axis of the leg-actuator entry points inside the chassis cylinder.
* Routing Constraints: Differential analog traces from the 12 spring displacement sensors must be strictly length-matched (under 45 mm) to equalize external noise exposure, maximizing the Common-Mode Rejection Ratio (CMRR) of the differential op-amps.

## 4. LAYER 3: High-Current Power & Bus Driver Layer (Power & Drivers)

* Vertical Clearance (To Bottom Shell): 1.0 mm (High-power buck regulators and TVS arrays are bonded directly to the bottom chassis shell using thermal tape).
* Thermal Management: Directs extreme joule heat generated during high-torque locomotion away from internal chips and dumps it into the ground, mud, or water through the bottom shell.
* Star Ground Topology: A solid 0.8 mm thick copper busbar is soldered onto the PCB within 5 mm of the main 24V battery negative input. Logic GND, Power GND, and Chassis Shield GND are branched radially from this single point to suppress ground bounce completely.

